From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 20:19:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build: detect ARM64EC and route install dirs to
 arm64ec-windows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The arm64ec-w64-mingw32-clang toolchain reports cpu_family() as
'aarch64' but generates ARM64EC hybrid PEs that need to live in
arm64ec-windows/ alongside other ARM64EC system DLLs (ntdll, kernel32,
ucrtbase, etc.) — installing them under aarch64-windows/ would conflict
with the pure-ARM64 builds.

Detect ARM64EC via the __arm64ec__ / _M_ARM64EC predefines and route
windows_native_install_dir / windows_builtin_install_dir to
arm64ec-windows/ when those are set.

Also fix util_bit.hpp: the toolchain defines BOTH __x86_64__ and
__arm64ec__, so x86 intrinsic detection must check ARM64EC first
(generated code is ARM64, not x86 — x86 intrinsics aren't usable).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Madeira-commit: 7ffb6827fd446cb05b73f91dc9694b243753d927
Rebased: resolved
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-dxmt-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 meson.build | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 0bddfcc..e2ce0f0 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -16,6 +16,16 @@ clangpp = meson.get_compiler('cpp', native: true)
 
 cpu_family = host_machine.cpu_family()
 
+# ARM64EC: arm64ec-w64-mingw32-clang reports cpu_family() = 'aarch64' but is
+# really an x86_64-callable hybrid PE — we need to install to arm64ec-windows
+# (matches our wine/build-arm64ec layout) rather than aarch64-windows.
+is_arm64ec = false
+if cpu_family == 'aarch64'
+  is_arm64ec = cpp.compiles(
+    '#if !defined(__arm64ec__) && !defined(_M_ARM64EC)\n#error not arm64ec\n#endif\nint main(void){return 0;}',
+    name: 'arm64ec target')
+endif
+
 dxmt_include_dirs = [
   './include',
   './libs'
@@ -180,12 +190,21 @@ if dxmt_crossbuild
     endif
     windows_builtin_install_dir = 'x86_64-windows'
   elif cpu_family == 'aarch64'
-    if wine_builtin_dll
-      windows_native_install_dir = 'aarch64-windows'
+    if is_arm64ec
+      if wine_builtin_dll
+        windows_native_install_dir = 'arm64ec-windows'
+      else
+        windows_native_install_dir = 'system32'
+      endif
+      windows_builtin_install_dir = 'arm64ec-windows'
     else
-      windows_native_install_dir = 'system32'
+      if wine_builtin_dll
+        windows_native_install_dir = 'aarch64-windows'
+      else
+        windows_native_install_dir = 'system32'
+      endif
+      windows_builtin_install_dir = 'aarch64-windows'
     endif
-    windows_builtin_install_dir = 'aarch64-windows'
   else
     error('invalid cpu family')
   endif
